{
  "raw": {
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504850/learning-designer": {
      "title": "Learning Designer",
      "description": "Learning Designer • Join a well-established and supportive team to shape exceptional learning experiences • UC Level 7, Salary Range $103,259 pa - $111,865 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time Fixed Term Opportunity Until April 2027 Job no: 504850 Work type: Professional Location: Bruce Categories: Student Support Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description About us: University of Canberra is more than a university, it’s a community committed to shaping a better world through education, research, and opportunity with a strong commitment to inclusivity and reducing inequalities. Our vibrant campus in Australia’s capital city is a hub of innovation & opportunity. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate outcomes and student support, UC values progress over perfection, inclusion over competition, and real‑world impact over prestige. If you’re looking for a career that matters, where you can belong, grow, and help shape what’s next, you’ll find your place at UC. About the opportunity: Our Learning and Teaching team is seeking a passionate and collaborative Learning Designer to work closely with academic subject matter experts and teaching staff to design, develop, and deliver engaging, high-quality learning experiences across a diverse range of courses and disciplines. The Learning Designer play a key role in creating sustainable, engaging, and evidence-based learning and assessment experiences that support student success. This is an exciting opportunity for an innovative educator and learning design professional who is passionate about student-centred learning, digital pedagogy, and the effective use of educational technologies to enhance learning outcomes. Key Responsibilities: Partner with academic staff and stakeholders to design and implement innovative learning solutions that enhance the student experience. Design high-quality learning activities, assessments, and educational resources grounded in contemporary learning design principles. Develop and publish engaging digital learning materials, including interactive online resources. Provide expert advice on learning design, digital pedagogy, and educational technologies. Support the development of inclusive, flexible, and student-centred learning experiences across a range of disciplines. Manage project timelines, identify delivery risks, and ensure successful completion of learning design projects. Collaborate effectively with colleagues across the University to achieve strategic learning and teaching outcomes. About you: Demonstrated experience in learning design, instructional design, educational development, or a related field. Strong knowledge of learning design principles for online, blended, and face-to-face learning environments. Understanding and experience with H5P is highly desirable. A team player with strong written and verbal communication skills. The ability to work collaboratively across multiple projects and disciplines in a dynamic environment to meet tight deadlines Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be explored on our “ Work at UC ” site which includes: Flexible working arrangements Family-friendly policies On campus Gym, Medical services, Cafes, Post office, Supermarket and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. Professional Development offerings (study assistance, corporate programs and discounts) Access to Employee Assistance Program and a corporate private Health Plan (Bupa) How to apply: Please apply with your CV only, no other documentation is required at this stage. Please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. Working rights: Applicants who wish to apply for this position must have valid working rights at the time of submission. For job specific information: please contact Steve Bath, Deputy Director, Learning & Teaching, Steve.Bath@canberra.edu.au For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, 18 October 2026 Advertised: 09 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504828/community-engagement-coordinator": {
      "title": "Community Engagement Coordinator",
      "description": "Community Engagement Coordinator • Help shape a healthier, more connected UC community • UC Level 6, Salary Range $93,704 pa - $100,871 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time, Continuing Opportunity (0.8FTE arrangements may also be considered) Job no: 504828 Work type: Professional Location: Bruce Categories: Administration, Marketing and Communications Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Help shape a healthier, more connected UC community UC Level 6, Salary Range $93,704 pa - $100,871 pa plus 17% Super Full Time, Continuing Opportunity (0.8FTE arrangements may also be considered) About us: University of Canberra is more than a university, it’s a community committed to shaping a better world through education, research, and opportunity with a strong commitment to inclusivity and reducing inequalities. Our vibrant campus in Australia’s capital city is a hub of innovation & opportunity. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate outcomes and student support, UC values progress over perfection, inclusion over competition, and real‑world impact over prestige. If you’re looking for a career that matters, where you can belong, grow, and help shape what’s next, you’ll find your place at UC. About the role: The University of Canberra is seeking a creative and energetic Community Engagement Coordinator to help connect students with the support, resources, and services available through the UC Medical & Counselling Centre. This is an exciting opportunity to play a pivotal role in promoting student health and wellbeing through meaningful campaigns, engaging events, innovative digital content, and collaborative partnerships across the University. You'll champion the Centre's services by engaging students, promoting wellbeing initiatives, and fostering greater awareness of available health and support resources. Key responsibilities include: Developing, coordinating and delivering health promotion campaigns, wellbeing initiatives, and community engagement activities. Planning and facilitating health-themed events and activities. Building and maintaining strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders. Collaborating in the development of innovative communication and engagement strategies. Creating, coordinating and distributing engaging digital and print promotional materials. Managing and maintaining online communications channels. About you: You thrive on managing multiple priorities, being efficient, exploring new ideas, challenging conventional approaches, and identifying fresh opportunities to connect students with health and wellbeing services. To be successful in this role, you'll have: Experience in community engagement, health promotion, communications, marketing, events, or a related field. Exceptional written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated experience coordinating events, campaigns, or engagement activities. Ability to build strong relationships with stakeholders. Digital literacy and proficiency with the ability to create engaging content across multiple platforms. Strong organisational skills with a proactive, solutions-focused mindset. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights at the time of submission. How to apply: Please apply with you Resume only, no other documentation is required at this stage. Please ensure you take the time to align your Resume with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview or task. For job specific information: please contact Sam Smith, Assistant Practice Manager - sam.smith@canberra.edu.au For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 18 October 2026 Advertised: 07 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504623/snow-scholarship-program-coordinator": {
      "title": "Snow Scholarship Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Snow Scholarship Program Coordinator • Help shape the future of the next generation of leaders • UC Level 6, Salary Range $93,705 pa - $100,871 pa pro rata + 17% Super • 3-day Part-Time Continuing Opportunity | Flexible Hours Job no: 504623 Work type: Professional Location: Bruce Categories: Administration, Student Support Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Help shape the future of the next generation of leaders UC Level 6, Salary Range $93,705 pa - $100,871 pa pro rata + 17% Super 3-day Part-Time Continuing Opportunity | Flexible Hours About us: Snow Scholarships have been co-created by Snow Foundation and the University of Canberra. Snow Foundation believes in the power of education to change lives and open doors – helping students realise their potential and grow into confident, purposeful leaders. In partnership with the University of Canberra, The Snow Foundation committed $20 million to back students who have big dreams and just need the support to get there. University of Canberra’s vision is that “Together we work to empower, connect and share knowledge with our people, cultures and places.” UC is part of the fabric of the local community, and we aim to challenge the status quo through the pursuit of excellence in teaching, learning and research. The University of Canberra is deeply committed to reducing inequalities and making university accessible for students regardless of their background. About the opportunity: From the partnership between University of Canberra and the Snow Foundation, the Snow Scholarship is a new and transformative program, now in its first year, supporting students from diverse or Indigenous backgrounds from Canberra and regional or rural NSW who are facing barriers to higher education. The program provides support for the entire duration of their degree providing financial and pastoral care support, leadership development, First Nations experiences and education, and more. It’s about changing lives and creating impact, nurturing the next generation of leaders. This is a great opportunity to join the Snow Scholarship team as the Snow Scholarship Program Coordinator and play a meaningful role in a groundbreaking scholarship program at the University of Canberra, helping change the lives of students and supporting them to achieve their potential. Position Description: Snow Scholarship Program Coordinator.pdf Key Responsibilities: Coordinate the day-to-day administration and support delivery of the Snow Scholarship Program. Build strong, trusted relationships with scholars and key stakeholders. Provide empathetic, responsive, and high-quality support to students. Coordinate program activities, communications, events, and key milestones. Occasional out-of-hours activity may be required for key events. Identify opportunities to improve the scholar experience and strengthen program delivery. About You: You are dynamic, empathetic, and impact-driven, with a genuine passion for supporting students and helping them thrive. You bring strong experience in student support or program coordination, exceptional attention to detail, and the ability to build trusted relationships with students and stakeholders. This position is more than a job; it’s an opportunity to be part of a transformative program that changes lives. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be explored on our “ Work at UC ” site which includes: Flexible working arrangements and Family-friendly policies On campus Gym, Medical services, Cafes, Post office, Supermarket and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. Professional Development offerings (study assistance, corporate programs and discounts) Innovative work environment with a diverse and inclusive culture Access to Employee Assistance Program and a corporate private Health Plan (Bupa) University of Canberra embodies its Values of Everyone’s invites, Narragunnawali, Change the World, Dare to be Curious and Walk together which we are proud. UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via Connected – A Decadal Strategy 2023-2032 . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. What we need from you: To be considered for this position, submit your application through the “Apply Now” tab with your CV and a cover letter outlining why you are a strong fit for this position. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview or a written assessment. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position must have valid working rights at the time of submission. The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, the successful candidate will be required to have or obtain a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For job specific information: please contact Claire Toepfer, Snow Scholarship Program Manager, claire.toepfer@canberra.edu.au . For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . If you would like to request a reasonable adjustment to the selection process, please feel free to contact us. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 18 October 2026 Advertised: 05 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504802/lecturer-in-human-nutrition-dietetics": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Human Nutrition / Dietetics",
      "description": "Lecturer in Human Nutrition / Dietetics • Make a meaningful contribution to the future of nutrition and dietetics • Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,803pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super (Pro-rata) • Part-time (0.4 FTE – 15 hours per week), 2 years Fixed Term Opportunity Job no: 504802 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Nutrition and Dietetics Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Make a meaningful contribution to the future of nutrition and dietetics Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,803pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super (Pro-rata) Part-time (0.4 FTE – 15 hours per week), 2 years Fixed Term Opportunity About us: At the University of Canberra, we’re a welcoming and connected academic community shaped by the people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. Our research focuses on real-world challenges, working alongside partners to create outcomes that matter, while our teaching builds confidence and capability for the future. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, UC is a place where you can grow ideas, contribute knowledge, and make a difference. About the role: We are seeking an enthusiastic and innovative Lecturer in Human Nutrition or Dietetics to join our Discipline of Nutrition and Dietetics. This fixed-term, part-time opportunity is ideal for an early-career academic who is committed to excellence in teaching, student engagement, and the scholarship of learning and teaching. In this rewarding role, you will contribute significantly to the delivery and development of undergraduate and postgraduate nutrition and dietetics education. As an Education Focused academic, you will be committed to student-centred learning and innovative teaching practices, while actively contributing to the scholarly and collegial life of the School and Faculty. Key responsibilities: In this role, you will: Convene units, lead and contribute to teaching and curriculum development Coordinate units and develop contemporary, evidence-based learning materials. Deliver engaging lectures, tutorials, practical classes, laboratories, seminars, and workshops. Support and mentor students through consultation and academic guidance. Develop innovative teaching approaches that enhance student engagement and learning outcomes. Contribute to work-integrated learning and industry engagement activities. About you: To be successful in this role, you will bring: Demonstrated experience in designing, coordinating, and delivering university teaching programs. Experience teaching across undergraduate and/or postgraduate education, including online and blended learning environments. Excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to build effective relationships with students, colleagues, and industry partners. Strong oral and written communication skills. A commitment to student success, innovation in teaching, and continuous improvement. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and workplace health and safety principles. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: A PhD (or enrolled and working towards PhD completion) in Human Nutrition or Dietetics (Highly desirable). Registration as a Nutritionist or Accredited Practising Dietitian (APD), or eligibility to obtain APD status through Dietitians Australia. Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights at the time of submission. The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au How to apply: Please apply with you CV only, no other documentation is required at this stage. Please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. For job specific information: please contact Ekavi Geourgouropoulou - Discipline Lead in Nutrition and Dietetics - Ekavi.Georgousopoulou@canberra.edu.au For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 18 October 2026 Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504779/lecturer-in-pharmacy": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Pharmacy",
      "description": "Lecturer in Pharmacy • Be part of shaping the future of pharmacy practice and workforce development • Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa pro rata plus 17% Super • 2 x Part-time roles (0.6FTE, 22.5 hrs per week), Continuing & Fixed Term Opportunities Job no: 504779 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Pharmacy Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Be part of shaping the future of pharmacy practice and workforce development Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa pro rata plus 17% Super 2 x Part-time roles (0.6FTE, 22.5 hrs per week), Continuing & Fixed Term Opportunities About us: Connected and inclusive, the University of Canberra works alongside the diverse people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. We deliver practical, real-world learning that helps students build confidence, skills and futures that matter. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, we’re shaping a better world through innovation, equity, and practical impact. Through our Reconnected Strategy , UC is committed to our purpose and values in leading the national education & research sector, championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility . The University of Canberra welcomes applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity, and individuals from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds.” About the opportunity: Australia is entering a new era of pharmacy practice, with pharmacist prescribing rapidly becoming a core component of healthcare delivery. 80% of community pharmacists are predicted to become qualified prescribers within the next decade, which presents an exciting opportunity for academic leaders to be part of shaping the future of pharmacy practice and workforce development. The University of Canberra is seeking 2x part-time (0.6FTE, 22.5 hrs per week), Lecturers in Pharmacy to join our Pharmacy discipline, one for a continuing role and the other for a 12-month fixed term contract. As a Lecturer in Pharmacy, you will play a key role in delivering and enhancing the University's pharmacy programs across face-to-face, online and blended learning environments. You will also have the opportunity to develop your scholarly profile through learning and teaching scholarship, educational innovation, and research supervision activities. Position Description - Lecturer in Pharmacy (Level B).pdf Position Description - Lecturer in Pharmacy (Level B) - FT.pdf Key Responsibilities: In this role, you will: Deliver engaging lectures, tutorials, workshops and practical classes across various learning modes. Coordinate units and contribute to curriculum development, assessment design and student learning experiences. Design and evaluate innovative, authentic assessments that support student success. Develop and maintain productive relationships with healthcare organisations, professional bodies, industry and community stakeholders. Contribute to research supervision where appropriate, including Honours, Masters and PhD students. About you: To be successful in this role, you will bring: Contemporary experience in pharmacy practice and a strong understanding of current developments within the profession. Experience in tertiary teaching, assessment and/or curriculum development in pharmacy or a related health discipline. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to be teaching and mentoring your industry peers. Completion of, or substantial progress towards, a PhD in pharmacy or a related field (Desirable). Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. Eligibility: A postgraduate qualification in pharmacy, clinical pharmacy, pharmacy practice, pharmacology or a related discipline. Current registration as a pharmacist with AHPRA. Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights at the time of submission. How to apply: To be considered for this position, we require your CV and a cover letter explaining your interest, you would bring to the role and your preference for either continuing or fixed-term employment. We kindly ask that you take this opportunity to align your CV with the Position Description, ensuring that your skills and experience are clearly articulated in connection with the specific requirements of the role. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. For job specific information: please contact Mary Bushell - Discipline Lead in Pharmacy - Mary.Bushell@canberra.edu.au - 02 6206 3934. For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 25 October 2026 Advertised: 25 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504729/lecturer-in-health": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Health",
      "description": "Lecturer in Health • Inspiring the next generation of health professionals • Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time, Continuing Opportunity Job no: 504729 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Health Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Inspiring the next generation of health professionals Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super Full Time, Continuing Opportunity About us: The University of Canberra is a welcoming and connected academic community shaped by its people, cultures and environments in Australia’s capital. Our research focuses on real-world challenges, working alongside partners to create outcomes that matter, while our teaching builds confidence and capability for the future. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, UC is a place where you can grow ideas, contribute knowledge, and make a difference. About the role: UC’s Faculty of Health is currently recruiting for a passionate Lecturer in Health (education focused) to join us to inspire and prepare graduates in the evolving health, disability, and community sectors. This is an exciting opportunity for an early career academic who is dedicated to student success and wishes to contribute meaningfully to innovative, high-quality health education. This role, plays a key part in delivering engaging learning experiences across interdisciplinary health programs, working collaboratively with colleagues to support student achievement and academic excellence. Key responsibilities include: Preparing and delivering high-quality classes Coordinating units and contributing to course management and quality assurance activities. Designing innovative and authentic assessment tasks that enhance student learning and graduate outcomes. Providing academic guidance, mentorship, and support to students. About you: To be successful in this role, you will be a collegial, scholarly and inquisitive educator driven to create a positive impact on the health professional eco-system. Teaching a broad Health Science skilled subject, you will help define, guide and influence student’s professional direction. Other requirements include: Professional experience within health, disability, community health, allied health, or closely related sectors. Experience applying professional practice knowledge to teaching and learning environments. Demonstrated ability to design, develop, coordinate, and deliver undergraduate and postgraduate subjects. Experience teaching in a health-related discipline within a tertiary education environment. Strong interpersonal, communication, and stakeholder management skills. Evidence of scholarly activity and the ability to translate contemporary research into engaging and relevant teaching practices. A PhD in Health or a related discipline Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights in Australia with the ability to start in early 2027. A current ACT working with vulnerable people (WWVP) registration, or ability to obtain. How to apply: Please apply with you CV only, no other documentation is required at this stage. Please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. For job specific information: please contact Alison Shield - Head of School - Health Sciences - alison.shield@canberra.edu.au - 02 6201 2084. For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Friday 23 October 2026 Advertised: 22 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504731/lecturer-in-public-health": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Public Health",
      "description": "Lecturer in Public Health • Shape Public Health Education • Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time, Continuing Opportunity Job no: 504731 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Shape Public Health Education Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super Full Time, Continuing Opportunity About us: At the University of Canberra, we believe education should be built for real people. People with different stories, responsibilities and ways of getting here. We are a modern Australian university focused on equal access to education and providing a supportive community where our students feel safe to grow and thrive. We support students as whole people, help them build confidence and prepare them to use their qualification in work, community and life beyond university. Working at UC means contributing to a university that puts people first. #UCan@UC About the role: UC is seeking for an engaged and enthusiastic Lecturer in Public Health (education focused) to join our Faculty of Health teaching into the Masters program. Working collaboratively with Health Research Institute (HRI) you will incorporate our cutting-edge research expertise into the educational programs and supporting student achievement and academic excellence. This role plays a critical part in shaping and delivering engaging learning experiences and promoting public health for a better tomorrow. Key responsibilities: Preparing and delivering high-quality classes Coordinating units and contributing to course management and quality assurance activities. Designing innovative and authentic assessment tasks that enhance student learning and graduate outcomes. Providing academic guidance, mentorship, and support to students. About you: You are an inspiring educator committed to student success and advancing community health in preparing the next generation of public health professionals. To be considered for the role you will also have: Experience applying professional practice knowledge to teaching and learning environments. Demonstrated ability to design, develop, coordinate, and deliver undergraduate and postgraduate subjects. Experience teaching in a health-related discipline within a tertiary education environment. Strong interpersonal, communication, and stakeholder management skills. Evidence of scholarly activity and the ability to translate contemporary research into engaging and relevant teaching practices. A PhD in Epidemiology or Public Health, or a related discipline. Professional experience within public health sector (advantageous). Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, pharmacy, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position will require Australian working rights with the ability to start in early 2027. A current ACT working with vulnerable people (WWVP) registration, or ability to obtain. How to apply: Please apply with you CV only, no other documentation is required at this stage. Please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. For job specific information: please contact Alison Shield - Head of School - Health Sciences - alison.shield@canberra.edu.au - 02 6201 2084. For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Friday 23 October 2026 Advertised: 22 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504740/lecturer-in-social-work": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Social Work",
      "description": "Lecturer in Social Work • Combine your social work expertise with a passion for teaching and student development • Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time, Continuing Opportunity Job no: 504740 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Combine your social work expertise with a passion for teaching and student development Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super Full Time, Continuing Opportunity About us: At the University of Canberra, we’re a welcoming and connected academic community shaped by the people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. Our research focuses on real-world challenges, working alongside partners to create outcomes that matter, while our teaching builds confidence and capability for the future. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, UC is a place where you can grow ideas, contribute knowledge, and make a difference. About the role: Due to rapid growth, our Faculty of Health is seeking an enthusiastic and student-centred Lecturer in Social Work (Education Focused) to join our growing Discipline of Social Work. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to the discipline and help shape the future of social work education through cutting-edge teaching, clinical supervision, and curriculum innovation. This dynamic and expanding program delivers high-quality teaching helping establish innovative social work services. This role is central to the course delivery and supporting student success through their degree in combining academic teaching with clinical education and supervision. Key responsibilities: In this role, you will: Deliver engaging teaching across the social work curriculum. Coordinate units and contribute to course leadership activities. Lead the development and implementation of a student-led Social Work Clinic. Collaborate to develop curriculum aligned with accreditation standards and contemporary social work practice. Build and maintain strong partnerships with community, health, and human service organisations. Contribute to scholarship and research in teaching and learning, particularly in social work education. About you: We are looking for an experienced social work professional who is passionate about education and committed to developing future practitioners. To be successful, you will have: A Master of Social Work (Qualifying) or equivalent qualification. A PhD in Social Work or a related discipline, or a willingness to undertake doctoral studies would be advantageous At least five years' professional social work experience. Membership (or eligibility) with the Australian Association of Social Workers (AASW). Demonstrated experience supervising students undertaking field education placements. Previous teaching experience in higher education, social work, or the human services sector. Evidence of teaching quality, educational innovation, or professional training delivery. Experience working collaboratively with stakeholders across health, community, or human services sectors with existing networks in the Act and region The ability to contribute to online, blended, and face-to-face learning environments. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights at the time of submission. The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au How to apply: Please apply with you CV and a cover letter outlining your interest and suitability. Also, please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. For job specific information: please contact Lynne Keevers, Professor in Social Work, Lynne.Keevers@canberra.edu.au - 02 6206 8652 or 0448641162. For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Tuesday 20 October 2026 Advertised: 22 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504696/lecturer-in-occupational-therapy": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Lecturer in Occupational Therapy We are growing out team! The University of Canberra is seeking occupational therapists with a commitment to excellence in education, clinical practice and research to join our highly regarded team. Job no: 504696 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Teaching and Research, Occupational Therapy Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description We are growing out team! The University of Canberra is seeking occupational therapists with a commitment to excellence in education, clinical practice and research to join our highly regarded team. Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super Full Time or Part-time, Continuing Opportunity About us: Connected and inclusive, the University of Canberra works alongside the diverse people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. We deliver practical, real-world learning that helps students build confidence, skills and futures that matter. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, we’re shaping a better world through innovation, equity, and practical impact. Through our Reconnected Strategy , UC is committed to our purpose and values in leading the national education & research sector, championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility . The University of Canberra welcomes applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity, and individuals from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. About the opportunity: The University of Canberra is recruiting for an enthusiastic and committed academic to join our occupational therapy team as a Education Focus (EF) or Education Research (ER) lecturer. This is an exciting opportunity to make an impactful and meaningful contribution to teaching, scholarship, and research within a growing and highly regarded health discipline. As part of our collaborative academic team, this position plays a key role in delivering high-quality learning experiences across our Bachelor and Master of Occupational Therapy programs. This is a great opportunity to shape curriculum, drive teaching innovation, and develop a research profile aligned with the priorities of the Occupational Therapy discipline. Key Responsibilities: In this role, you will: Coordinate and deliver occupational therapy units. Lead innovative teaching practices. Prepare and deliver lectures, tutorials, workshops, practical classes, and seminars. Design, develop and review curriculum and learning materials. Assess student performance and provide high-quality feedback. Support student learning and supervise Honours and Higher Degree by Research (HDR) students (ER). Develop and contribute to a collaborative research program (ER). About you: To be successful, you will bring: Registration as an occupational therapist with AHPRA. Significant clinical experience as an occupational therapist. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching and student-centred learning. Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to engage diverse student cohorts. For Education Research role: PhD (or progress towards completion) An emerging or established research profile relevant to occupational therapy (for the research focused role option). Additional qualities that would be highly regarded include: Experience working with children and young people and/ or with within the disability sector Previous teaching, course coordination or supervision experience in higher education. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be explored on our “ Work at UC ” site which includes: Flexible working arrangements Family-friendly policies On campus Gym, Medical services, Cafes, Post office, Supermarket and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. Professional Development offerings (study assistance, corporate programs and discounts) Access to Employee Assistance Program and a corporate private Health Plan (Bupa) What we need from you: To be considered for this position, we require your CV and a cover letter explaining what skills and experience you would bring to the role and why you are interested in the position. How to apply: Please apply with you CV and a cover letter outlining your interest and suitability. Also, please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. Position Description - Lecturer in Occupational Therapy (EF) Position Description - Lecturer in Occupational Therapy (ER) Working rights: Applicants who wish to apply for this position must have valid working rights at the time of submission. WWVP: The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au For job specific information: please contact Claire Pearce - Discipline Lead in Occupational Therapy - Claire.Pearce@canberra.edu.au - 02 6206 8452. For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 18 October 2026 Advertised: 18 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504732/lecturer-in-physiotherapy": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Physiotherapy",
      "description": "Lecturer in Physiotherapy • Shape the future of physiotherapy education and practice. • Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time, Continuing Opportunity Job no: 504732 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Teaching and Research, Physiotherapy Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Shape the future of physiotherapy education and practice. Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super Full Time, Continuing Opportunity About us: At the University of Canberra, we’re a welcoming and connected academic community shaped by the people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. Our research focuses on real-world challenges, working alongside partners to create outcomes that matter, while our teaching builds confidence and capability for the future. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, UC is a place where you can grow ideas, contribute knowledge, and make a difference. About the role: Due to the Discipline of Physiotherapy discipline growing in size, reach and research, UC is seeking two passionate and experienced Physiotherapists to join as Education Focused Lecturers. These exciting opportunities provide the chance to contribute to the education of future health professionals while maintaining strong connections with contemporary clinical practice and research. We are recruiting for two discipline-specific appointments: Lecturer in Physiotherapy (Musculoskeletal Physiotherapy) Lecturer in Physiotherapy (Neurological Physiotherapy) Key responsibilities include: Collaboratively developing, delivering and evaluating undergraduate and postgraduate physiotherapy Accredited curriculum Preparing and delivering lectures, tutorials, practical classes, workshops, demonstrations and professional placement activities Supporting student learning, engagement and wellbeing Contributing to research and scholarly activities aligned with the Discipline's strategic priorities About you: You are an enthusiastic Physiotherapist with a passion for education and developing the next generation of clinicians. You bring contemporary clinical expertise, strong communication skills and a collaborative approach to teaching and professional engagement. The successful candidate will have the following desirable qualifications and experience: Expertise in person-centred and inclusive physiotherapy practice Experience managing complex clients across a range of clinical environments and caseloads Honours to PhD in the following discipline would be advantageous, or 5 years clinical experience: Musculoskeletal Physiotherapy (for the Musculoskeletal-focused role), or Neurological Physiotherapy (for the Neurological-focused role) Experience supervising, mentoring or delivering clinical education to students or early-career clinicians Demonstrated capacity to design, develop, coordinate and deliver evidence-based clinical learning experiences that align with AHPRA standards Excellent written and verbal communication skills Research training or experience, including research design, critical appraisal and basic statistical methods Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Current registration as a Physiotherapist with AHPRA The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au How to apply: Please apply with you CV and a cover letter (max 2 pages) outlining your interest and suitability against the key responsibilities listed on the Position Description . If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. For job specific information: please contact Phillip Newman - Discipline Lead in Physiotherapy - phillip.newman@canberra.edu.au - 02 6201 2831. For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Friday 16, October 2026. Advertised: 16 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/737/cw/en/job/500806/sessional-staff-talent-pool-faculty-of-arts-and-design": {
      "title": "Sessional Staff Talent Pool Faculty Of Arts And Design",
      "description": "Casual Academic Staff Talent Pool - Faculty of Arts and Design Upload your CV to register for academic sessional positions Job no: 500806 Work type: Academic, Casual Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Teaching and Research, Architecture and Design Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results Do you wish to be contacted when a position becomes available that meets your skills? The Faculty of Arts and Design offers a range of courses that encompasses everything creative, and we work with our students to bring their concepts and ideas into practical reality. Academic sessional positions include a range of duties including, but not limited to, tutoring; marking; demonstrating; teaching; student outreach and engagement; moderating/facilitating, and/or student advising; across multiple academic disciplines. Please note by joining our Talent Pool you will not be automatically considered for advertised vacancies. To register , please complete the online application form along with your CV and submit it to ensure your application is complete. If your personal details or your situation changes, please note you will be able to update your application as needed. Advertised: 19 Feb 2024 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/737/cw/en/job/500555/sessional-staff-talent-pool-faculty-of-business-government-law": {
      "title": "Sessional Staff Talent Pool Faculty Of Business Government Law",
      "description": "Casual Academic Staff Talent Pool - Faculty of Business Government & Law Upload your CV to register for academic sessional and casual positions Job no: 500555 Work type: Academic, Casual Academic, Casual Professional Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Research Only, Teaching and Research Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results Do you wish to be contacted when a position becomes available that meets your skills? The Faculty of Business, Government & Law is committed to providing an outstanding student experience, where teaching and learning are delivered by exceptional teachers and researchers in sectors where our students enjoy the best employment outcomes in the ACT following graduation. Our teaching and research are focused particularly in the nexus between business and government. Academic sessional positions include a range of duties including (but are not limited to) tutoring; marking; demonstrating; teaching; student outreach and engagement; moderating/facilitating and/or student advising; across multiple academic disciplines. Please note by joining our Talent Pool you will not be automatically considered for advertised vacancies. To register , please complete the online application form along with your CV and submit it to ensure your application is complete. If your personal details or your situation changes, please note you will be able to update your application as needed. Advertised: 19 Feb 2024 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/737/cw/en/job/500807/sessional-staff-talent-pool-faculty-of-education": {
      "title": "Sessional Staff Talent Pool Faculty Of Education",
      "description": "Casual Academic Staff Talent Pool - Faculty of Education Upload your CV to register for academic sessional positions Job no: 500807 Work type: Academic, Casual Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Research Only, Teaching and Research, Education Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results Do you wish to be contacted when a position becomes available that meets your skills? The Faculty of Education offers undergraduate and graduate entry courses in early childhood, primary and secondary teacher education; postgraduate education and educational leadership; and postgraduate Teaching English to Speakers of Other Languages (TESOL) courses. It also offers Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) and Doctor of Education (EdD) programs. All of the Faculty’s Initial Teacher Education courses have a significant, school-based, clinical component. Academic sessional positions include a range of duties including, but not limited to, tutoring; marking; demonstrating; teaching; student outreach and engagement; moderating/facilitating, and/or student advising; across multiple academic disciplines. Please note by joining our Talent Pool you will not be automatically considered for advertised vacancies. To register , please complete the online application form along with your CV and submit it to ensure your application is complete. If your personal details or your situation changes, please note you will be able to update your application as needed. Advertised: 19 Feb 2024 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/737/cw/en/job/500808/sessional-staff-talent-pool-faculty-of-health": {
      "title": "Sessional Staff Talent Pool Faculty Of Health",
      "description": "Casual Academic Staff Talent Pool - Faculty of Health Upload your CV to register for academic sessional positions Job no: 500808 Work type: Academic, Casual Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Research Only, Teaching and Research, Health Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results Do you wish to be contacted when a position becomes available that meets your skills? The Faculty of Health is a dynamic hub comprising three Schools housing a diverse array of health and sports disciplines, from Nursing, Midwifery, and Physiotherapy to Sport and Exercise Science, Nutrition, and more. With a focus on innovative education methods, the faculty is continuously evolving with the environment and producing high-quality, work-ready graduates and leading health research. Academic sessional positions include a range of duties including, but not limited to, tutoring; marking; demonstrating; teaching; student outreach and engagement; moderating/facilitating, and/or student advising; across multiple academic disciplines. Please note by joining our Talent Pool you will not be automatically considered for advertised vacancies. To register , please complete the online application form along with your CV and submit it to ensure your application is complete. If your personal details or your situation changes, please note you will be able to update your application as needed. Advertised: 19 Feb 2024 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/737/cw/en/job/500809/sessional-staff-talent-pool-faculty-of-science-and-technology": {
      "title": "Sessional Staff Talent Pool Faculty Of Science And Technology",
      "description": "Casual Academic Staff Talent Pool - Faculty of Science and Technology Upload your CV to register for academic sessional positions Job no: 500809 Work type: Academic, Casual Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Research Only, Teaching and Research, Science - Biomedical, Science - Environmental Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results Do you wish to be contacted when a position becomes available that meets your skills? The Faculty of Science and Technology ’s focus spans across environmental science, data science, IT, engineering, robotics, cybersecurity, biomedical, and more, ensuring a dynamic balance between theory and hands-on practice for students, epitomizing our commitment to innovation and excellence in research and education. Academic sessional positions include a range of duties including, but not limited to, tutoring; marking; demonstrating; teaching; student outreach and engagement; moderating/facilitating, and/or student advising; across multiple academic disciplines. Please note by joining our Talent Pool you will not be automatically considered for advertised vacancies. To register , please complete the online application form along with your CV and submit it to ensure your application is complete. If your personal details or your situation changes, please note you will be able to update your application as needed. Advertised: 19 Feb 2024 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
